\item A steady-state constant infusion (\code{ss = 1}, \code{amt = 0}, \code{rate > 0}).
\item A negative \code{rate} or \code{dur}: NONMEM's \code{-1} and \code{-2} say the rate or
the duration is a model parameter, and an estimated duration moves
where the solve is split, which \code{\link[=frm_ode]{frm_ode()}} cannot do.
\item A dose with both a positive \code{rate} and a positive \code{dur}.
\item A \code{rate}, \code{dur}, \code{ii}, \code{addl} or \code{ss} that is not finite on an
event, or that is nonzero on an observation; an \code{amt}, \code{ii},
\code{addl} or \code{ss} that is nonzero on a reset (\code{evid = 3}). The split
would drop each of them without a word.
\item A \code{cmt} on a dose that is missing, zero or below, or not a whole
number.
\item An \code{mdv} column that disagrees with \code{evid}. \code{mdv = 1} on an
\code{evid = 0} row is a missing observation, which would otherwise
become a fitted one.
